{
  "name": "token-exp-leeway",
  "description": "Fresh assertions at and just outside the exp boundary (t < exp + 30 s), each signed with its iat before the service's clock t. iat = t - 75 (exp 15 s in the past, inside the leeway): accepted. iat = t - 89 (exp + 30 s is t + 1 s): accepted. iat = t - 90 (exp + 30 s is exactly t): invalid_client. With exp - iat = 30, iat = t - 59: accepted, and iat = t - 60 (exp + 30 s is exactly t): invalid_client, though iat is only 60 s old: the boundary is on exp, not on iat.",
